# f3 — built FROM SOURCE via a novadeck-owned PKGBUILD (packages/f3/PKGBUILD), NOT fetched from the
# holo monorepo: f3 is an AUR package, absent from both holo and the upstream aarch64 base, so there
# is no repo row to resolve and no upstream PKGBUILD to pull. Same "local PKGBUILD" form as
# packages/gtk2/source.pin.
#
# Why: the client's format dialog offers "Run validation tests", ticked by default for SD media, and
# f3probe is the test. See the PKGBUILD header for why only ONE of upstream's five binaries is
# built, and usr/lib/novadeck/storage/format-device.sh for how the verdict is read (f3probe exits 0
# even for a counterfeit card — the answer is in its stdout).
#
# Version: 10.0, upstream's latest release. The reference platform pins 8.0.
#
# Fields (see packages/README.md):
#   name           pkgname (must match the PKGBUILD); also the work/ build-dir + repo entry
#   pkgbuild_local path (relative to this dir) to the checked-in PKGBUILD to build
#   pkgrel_suffix  numeric suffix appended to the PKGBUILD's pkgrel so pacman prefers our build
#
# To bump f3: edit pkgver + sha256sums in packages/f3/PKGBUILD, and re-check that
# `build/f3probe` is still a Makefile target and still links only -lm -ludev — a release that moved
# f3probe onto libparted would silently pull parted onto the image through depends.
name: f3
pkgbuild_local: PKGBUILD
pkgrel_suffix: 1
